ZTEXT001000007b5f44e113b0000000
NATIVE ZERO PICTURE COMMAND

tools/picture.zero is the original Zero implementation for Linux x86-64 and
Windows x64. It invokes no process, external image codec or language runtime.

  zero-picture make INPUT.ppm NEW.zpix
  zero-picture verify FILE.zpix
  zero-picture read FILE.zpix NEW.ppm
  zero-picture raw FILE.zpix NEW.rgb

The P6 PPM import/export and raw RGB output are explicit interoperability
operations. Project image assets use our own .zpix container. The native
command does not open a window and is not a desktop image viewer.

P6 import requires decimal dimensions within 1..3840 by 1..2160, maxval 255,
three bytes per pixel and an exact raster length. Comments and whitespace are
accepted between header tokens. The final raster separator is one whitespace
byte or CRLF; an initial LF pixel after a single CR separator is preserved by
checking the exact expected raster size. Extra frames, trailing bytes, other
PPM encodings, 16-bit channels and incomplete RGB rasters are rejected.

Validation finishes before any output path is opened. Existing paths are
refused. New outputs are written completely, flushed and closed; a failed
write/flush/close removes only the newly created partial file. Input sources
are never changed. File flushing does not promise directory-metadata durability.

The native command owns 67112960 bytes of workspace. It reads at most 32 MiB,
checks exact file size and premature EOF, and rejects a detected size change.
Do not modify an input concurrently; same-size edits are not an atomic snapshot.
Format bounds and reusable decoder contract are specified in media/ZPIX.ztext.

To recompose the shared decoder using only our own native Zero tool:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_PICTURE.zero --picture
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_CHECK.zero --picture-check

The original Zero regression executable is zero-picture-check. The native
builder emits Linux/Windows command and regression executables together.
